# stereo_spin: stereo as a spinor, every stereo move one rotation
# (notes/spinors-2026-11-05.md, "Stereo is already a spinor").
#
# Make each side analytic and the pair [L, R] is two complex numbers,
# (xi, eta): a spinor (in optics, a Jones vector). Its Hopf map is the
# state of the stereo image, a point on a sphere:
#   S1 = |L|^2 - |R|^2           balance, left against right
#   S2 + i S3 = 2 conj(L) R      correlation: in phase (S2), in quadrature (S3)
# A mono sound at the centre sits at +S2. Every stereo move is a turn of
# that sphere, and every turn is a pair of pairs acting on the spinor by
# Hamilton's product (SPEC "Pairs of pairs"):
#   about S3   equal-power panning; a quarter turn is hard left or right,
#              half a turn is the sides in anti-phase, and a quarter turn
#              from the centre the other way is mid/side
#   about S1   the sides' phases spread apart: in phase, then quadrature
#              (a frequency-free 90 degrees, the Hilbert pair), then
#              anti-phase
#   about S2   balance traded for quadrature
# The three are composed by his product into one rotation and played as
# the real parts of the turned spinor. With every turn at 0 the sound is
# the source, through the Hilbert pair (clean above about 30 Hz).
#
# Playing it (tools/pad; each knob starts at 0, no turn, and goes round a
# full circle as it rises):
#   A + left/right   turn about S3: centre, right, anti-phase, left, centre
#   A + up/down      turn about S1: in phase, quadrature, anti-phase, ...
#   B + up/down      turn about S2
#   tools/pad & AITHER_MIDI=aither-pad ./aither patches/stereo_spin.aither | tools/play hw:rockchipes8388c 20
# On a scope the image is drawn as it turns: ... | tools/play hw:rockchipes8388c 20 | tools/scope

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the turns

# The image's sphere in Hamilton's units: balance (S1) is i, quadrature
# (S3) is j, in phase (S2) is k, each turned the other way round
# (about(-axis, w) is about(axis, -w)).
let w3 = slew(midi_cc(21), 0.05) * TAU                    # about S3
let w1 = slew(midi_cc(20), 0.05) * TAU                    # about S1
let w2 = slew(midi_cc(22), 0.05) * TAU                    # about S2
let r = about(j, -w3) * about(i, -w1) * about(k, -w2)      # the whole turn

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- a sound

# A warm tone, struck softly every 1.4 s, with a breath of noise: mono,
# so it starts at the centre of the sphere.
let strike = impulse(1 / 1.4)
def push(trig): (discharge(trig, 1 / 0.001) - discharge(trig, 1 / 0.0003)) / 0.0007
# Each mode is pushed by its share over 2 pi f, so it rings at that share
# (a resonator rings a push of area P at P times 2 pi f).
let body = sum(5, n =>
  let f = 196 * n * (1 + 0.0007 * n * n)
  resonator(push(strike) * 0.12 / n / (TAU * f), f, 2 / (2.5 / n)))
let tone = additive(196, warm_shape, 6) * (0.10 + 0.05 * sin(TAU * t / 7))
let breath = bpf(noise(), 1800, 0.4) * 0.03
let src = body + tone + breath

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- the spinor

# [L, R], each analytic (the same: centred), as Hamilton writes a spinor
# for his product to turn: L + (-conj(R)) j, so its second half is
# -conj(R), and the turned R is minus the real part of the second half.
let side = analytic(src)
let ((l, _), (minus_r, _)) = r * (side, conj(side) * -1)

[l, -minus_r] |> reverb(1.4, 0.1)
